{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/919479-gming-a-game-and-need-some-thoughts-on-the-strix","id":919479,"title":"Gming a game and need some thoughts on the Strix","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-22T20:14:04-07:00","id":919479,"title":"Gming a game and need some thoughts on the Strix","content":"I'm making a game for my friends, all are veteran players and i'm a brand new GM. I was reading rulebooks when I came across the Strix. I'd like to make one an antag but how would i make one. I have little experience with ghosts, but from what I was reading they don't translate to the same thing, but it is good to know ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T01:09:38-07:00","id":919582,"title":"","content":"I'm not quite sure what your problem with making a Strix NPC is. Could you elaborate? Also, are you using VtR 2e a.k.a. Blood and Smoke?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T02:37:04-07:00","id":919605,"title":"","content":"I believe there should be a section in 2nd Edition Vampire: the Requiem where they go over the creation process for the Strix. As for suggestions, first decide how powerful you want the Strix to be. A low Shadow Potency one will only be able to really possess corpses or torpored Kindred. Higher level ones can posses waking Kindred and even the living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T05:21:45-07:00","id":919649,"title":"","content":"I have the books, i'm just confused on how to set up it's basic attributes. Also as well with the Strix can they move through walls or is it they pour through cracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T07:43:18-07:00","id":919705,"title":"","content":"Shadow Potency determines how many dots you can allocate to Attributes, but instead of a precise value, it's a range, e.g 4-6 for SP1 and 7-10 for SP2. Just pick any number from this range - the higher the number, the stronger the Strix will be, so you get some extra customization within each rank to better match the needs of your campaign. Don't worry too much about getting the number just right - if your team can survive a Strix with SP2 and 8 dots of Attributes, it should also survive one with 10 dots of Attributes.<br /> <br /> Unless they have the Twilight Form Embodiment, the Strix are material (but intangible). They can slip through the tiniest crack, but a hermetically sealed room is out of their reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T10:29:38-07:00","id":919797,"title":"","content":"The Strix literally <b>are </b>shadows and smoke, so they can do all the things you expect creatures of shadows and smoke to be able to.<br /> <br /> As for power level... it really comes down to what role the Strix is supposed to play in the story, from what position it acts and with what goals. It is hard to give a definitive answer without more context about the player characters and the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T19:28:37-07:00","id":920091,"title":"","content":"Here's some backstory. It takes place in LA and the vamps are actually in a good position. The fledglings though ruin the fun of the night by unleashing a strix that has been trapped. It's in a new city, it's old, and it has a fresh hatred for Kindred and there use of humanity. The players are the fledglings and are all vet players making 2 grapple, 1 ranged, and a social, but they have never fought strix. How should I set this up, as one adores obsfucate, another loves to shoot first ask questions never. How should I use the Strix as antag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T19:49:41-07:00","id":920097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/919479-gming-a-game-and-need-some-thoughts-on-the-strix?p=920091#post920091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's some backstory. It takes place in LA and the vamps are actually in a good position. The fledglings though ruin the fun of the night by unleashing a strix that has been trapped. It's in a new city, it's old, and it has a fresh hatred for Kindred and there use of humanity. The players are the fledglings and are all vet players making 2 grapple, 1 ranged, and a social, but they have never fought strix. How should I set this up, as one adores obsfucate, another loves to shoot first ask questions never. How should I use the Strix as antag</div> </div> </div> </div>Strix are meant to be an out of context problem. They're not something vampires can easily deal with. Take advantage of that. It sounds like in this situation having the strix go full bodyjacker would be an excellent way for it to harass them. They can kill its host bodies all the time, but it will find others and leave them to clean up the mess until they start playing things smart. There you can have some sort of research or investigations allowed that would let them find its banes, perhaps having them come up during encounters with it, and maybe lead them to imprisoning it in a bottle or something which they can bury or hide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-23-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:48:25-07:00","id":920424,"title":"","content":"I like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}